  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Anr vs Union Of India & Ors on 17 December, 2014 Author: I. P. Mukerji Bench: I. P. Mukerji Wp No.1097 of 2014 In The High Court At Calcutta Constitutional Writ Jurisdiction Original Side Flemingo Dutyfree Shop Pvt. Ltd. & Anr. -Versus- Union Of India & Ors. Appearance: Mr. J.K. Khaitan, Sr. Adv. Mr. K.R. Thakkar, Adv. ...for the petitioner. Mr. Pradip Kumar Roy, Adv. Mr. K.K. Maity, Adv. ...for the respondent.",
    "facts": "Consignments of these alcoholic beverages covered by bill of entry No.7089742 dated 16th October, 2014 and bill of entry No.7107353 dated 18th October, 2014 are held up by the Customs Department. They want to test the goods under Section 25 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. This is resisted by the writ petitioner company on several grounds.",
    "arguments": "Mr. Khaitan, learned senior Advocate submits that sales tax or VAT is also not payable. Mr. Khaitan, learned senior Advocate contends that these goods cannot be termed as 'imported'. They do not pass through the customs barrier. That these goods are not imported have been noted by the Bombay High Court in their decision in the case of DFS India Pvt. Ltd. & Anr. vs. Union of India & Ors. decided on 27th August, 2014, by a Division Bench. The goods neither attract Customs duty nor any sales tax. Hence, according to Mr. Khaitan, the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 does not have any application with regard to the goods.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Mr. Khaitan, learned senior Advocate submits that sales tax or VAT is also not payable. Mr. Khaitan, learned senior Advocate contends that these goods cannot be termed as 'imported'. They do not pass through the customs barrier. The goods neither attract Customs duty nor any sales tax. Hence, according to Mr. Khaitan, the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 does not have any application with regard to the goods.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "That these goods are not imported have been noted by the Bombay High Court in their decision in the case of DFS India Pvt. Ltd. & Anr. vs. Union of India & Ors. decided on 27th August, 2014, by a Division Bench."
  },
